WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.144
The saved school outline lists a 60-second tourniquet competency, burns, heat and cold, altitude syndromes, submersion, crush, complex trauma and a rapid load-and-go decision.
学校保存的纲要列出60秒止血带考核、烧伤、冷热、海拔综合征、浸没、挤压伤、复杂创伤及快速装车决策。

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:23.280
The stopwatch values are station benchmarks. They do not replace correct indication, safety, effective treatment, team communication or clinical judgment.
秒表数值是站点基准，不可替代正确适应症、安全、有效处理、团队沟通或临床判断。

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:35.184
Use the school’s own equipment and rubric under instructor supervision. This lesson prepares your reasoning; it does not certify a procedure or reproduce an assessed checkoff answer.
应在教师监督下使用学校器材及评分标准。本课帮助准备推理，但不能认证操作，也不会复现考核站点答案。

00:00:35.184 --> 00:00:57.336
The live school lab summary specifies application, cessation of bleeding and time-marking in under sixty seconds. Keep that less-than boundary for the station, rather than silently changing it to sixty seconds or less. This is an integrated supervised skill target, not permission to omit assessment or an effective bleeding check.
学校现行实操摘要规定，在少于60秒内完成应用、出血停止及时间标记。站点应保留“小于”边界，不能悄悄改成“小于或等于60秒”。这是受监督整合技能目标，不允许省略评估或有效止血检查。

00:00:57.336 --> 00:01:12.360
Current BCEHS PR03 applies to severe extremity bleeding when the indicated prior method has not controlled it; it requires complete bleeding control and documentation of application time. Follow the actual local procedure.
BCEHS现行PR03适用于符合条件且既有方法未能控制的严重肢体出血；要求完全止血并记录应用时间。应遵循实际当地操作规范。

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:25.920
During supervised practice, use the school’s specified trainer and technique. The instructor should confirm placement, securement, windlass/locking method, reassessment and documentation.
监督练习时使用学校指定训练器及手法。教师应确认位置、固定、旋杆/锁定方式、复评及记录。

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:36.624
A fast incomplete application is not a pass. Confirm the expected station rubric, then practise until the effective sequence is both accurate and repeatable.
快速但不完整的应用不算通过。应核实站点评分标准，反复练习直到有效步骤准确且可重复。

00:01:36.624 --> 00:02:06.360
For supervised practice with the approved windlass trainer, identify uncontrolled external limb bleeding and follow the current procedure’s direct-pressure attempt. If ineffective, place the device on skin, five to eight centimetres above the injury or high on the limb, avoiding a joint. Tighten the strap, then the windlass until bleeding stops; secure the windlass. The instructor checks technique and actual effect, not just completion of movements.
使用获准旋杆式训练器受监督练习时，先识别未控制肢体外出血，并依现行操作尝试直接加压。无效时，使器材接触皮肤，置于伤口近心端5至8厘米或肢体高位，避开关节。收紧束带，再转紧旋杆至出血停止，并固定旋杆。教师检查的是手法及真实效果，不只是做完动作。

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:32.904
Record the actual application time and procedure, reassess bleeding and the patient, and communicate the intervention. PR03 calls for consultation if management or transport may extend beyond two hours; that is not an instruction to loosen or remove the device at a timer. In class, practise correct placement and repeated assessment on the trainer, using the school’s device and checkoff requirements.
记录真实应用时间及操作，复评出血与患者，并交接干预。PR03要求，若现场处理或转运可能超过两小时，应取得咨询；这不是计时一到就松开或移除的指令。应在训练器上排练位置及复评，并使用学校器材与考核要求。

00:02:32.904 --> 00:02:46.320
In this original practice case, a sixty-one-year-old is brought from a detached workshop fire. The patient has a hoarse voice, cough and soot around the lips, with a visible partial-thickness forearm injury.
本原创练习中，一名61岁患者从独立车间火灾中被救出，出现声音嘶哑、咳嗽、唇周烟灰及前臂部分皮层烧伤。

00:02:46.320 --> 00:03:01.752
Treat the changing voice and soot as airway-risk information. Continue ABC assessment, consider combustion exposure and follow current H10, B01 and J02 guidance within the authorized provider role.
应把声音变化及烟灰视为气道风险线索。继续ABC评估、考虑燃烧暴露，并按执业角色遵循H10、B01及J02现行指导。

00:03:01.752 --> 00:03:15.480
Use the Rule of Nines or a suitable hand method to communicate an estimate of partial/deeper burn area. Superficial erythema is excluded from BCEHS TBSA, and the estimate is not exact.
可用九分法或适当手掌法沟通部分/更深烧伤面积估值。BCEHS TBSA不计表浅红斑，估值也不是精确值。

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:33.096
The school outline calls CO-oximetry mandatory in every enclosed fire. Current BCEHS J02 supports oxygen and consultation for suspected CO, while available CO-oximetry is an adjunct; do not teach the school phrase as a universal prerequisite.
学校纲要称每起封闭火灾都必须做CO-oximetry。BCEHS现行J02对疑似CO暴露支持给氧与咨询，可用CO-oximetry作辅助；不能把学校措辞教成通用前提。

00:03:33.096 --> 00:04:00.312
Use the adult Rule of Nines as an approximate model: head and neck nine percent, each complete arm nine, each complete leg eighteen, front trunk eighteen, back trunk eighteen, and perineum one. The linked BCEHS chart also offers a more detailed subunit method with different allocations. Choose and state one suitable method, rather than mixing its numbers with nines or applying adult proportions to a child.
成人九分法是近似模型：头颈9%，每条完整上肢9%，每条完整下肢18%，躯干前面18%、后面18%，会阴1%。BCEHS链接图还提供分配不同的细分区域方法。应选择并注明一种合适方法，不能把其数字与九分法混搭，也不能把成人比例套给儿童。

00:04:00.312 --> 00:04:31.608
Depth changes what you count. Superficial injury is limited to the epidermis, often red and dry. Partial-thickness injury extends into dermis; superficial partial injury commonly blisters and weeps, while deeper injury may be patchy or less sensitive. Full-thickness injury destroys dermis and may look leathery or charred with reduced sensation. Appearance evolves: record findings and uncertainty rather than diagnosing depth from pain alone.
深度决定计入哪些面积。表浅伤限于表皮，常红且干燥；部分皮层伤进入真皮，浅部分皮层常起疱渗液，较深者可能斑驳或感觉减弱；全层伤破坏真皮，可呈皮革样或焦黑并感觉减弱。外观会演变，应记录发现及不确定性，不能只凭疼痛确定深度。

00:04:31.608 --> 00:05:02.328
For an explicitly fictional update to the fire case, the whole left arm now has partial-thickness findings, while front-trunk redness is superficial only. Using adult nines, count nine percent, not nine plus eighteen. This is a teaching update, not a fact from the original patient description. Report the method, depth and estimate; ongoing hoarseness and soot still make airway and toxic exposure urgent, and the number does not prescribe a fluid dose.
给火灾案例增加一项明确虚构的教学变化：整个左上肢有部分皮层损伤发现，躯干前面只是表浅红斑。按成人九分法应计9%，不是9加18。这是教学变化，不是原患者描述中已有事实。应报告方法、深度及估值；持续嘶哑及烟灰仍使气道和毒物暴露紧急，数字不构成输液剂量。

00:05:02.328 --> 00:05:16.824
A twenty-eight-year-old climber at three thousand three hundred metres has a worsening headache and now cannot walk a straight line. There is no resting dyspnea reported. This is an original practice case, not the saved school case.
一名28岁登山者在海拔3300米处头痛加重，现在无法直线行走。没有报告静息呼吸困难。本例为原创练习，不是学校保存案例。

00:05:16.824 --> 00:05:31.080
New ataxia or altered mental status raises concern for high-altitude cerebral edema. Ask about ascent and sleep altitude, assess neurologic and respiratory status, and look for alternative causes.
新发共济失调或精神状态改变令人担忧高原脑水肿。应询问上升路线及睡眠海拔，评估神经与呼吸状态，并考虑其他病因。

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:42.024
Resting dyspnea, cough or worsening oxygenation would raise concern for HAPE, but its absence does not make HACE safe. Avoid further ascent and reduce exertion.
静息呼吸困难、咳嗽或氧合恶化会增加HAPE担忧；但没有这些表现并不代表HACE安全。应避免继续上升并减少活动。

00:05:42.024 --> 00:05:55.536
Urgent descent is central for severe altitude illness. If oxygen is available and indicated, start it while organizing safe descent; neither action should be delayed solely to complete the other.
严重高原病的关键是紧急下降。若现场有氧气且有指征，应在组织安全下降时同时给氧；不能仅为先完成另一项而延误。

00:05:55.536 --> 00:06:09.888
Compare a person who feels faint and sweaty after prolonged exertion with one who is confused and hot. Altered mental status with heat exposure raises a high-consequence concern and needs the current hyperthermia pathway.
比较一位长时间活动后头晕出汗者，与一位高热且混乱者。热暴露伴意识异常是高风险线索，应使用现行高热路径。

00:06:09.888 --> 00:06:22.728
Current BCEHS I02 calls for prompt cooling and continuation during transport when possible. Choose a method that remains safe for the patient’s mobility, airway, trauma and the crew.
BCEHS现行I02要求尽可能及时降温，并在转运中继续；选择方法时须考虑患者活动能力、气道、创伤及团队安全。

00:06:22.728 --> 00:06:36.144
For cold exposure, remove the person from further cooling, dry and insulate, and handle gently. Peripheral thermometer readings are imperfect; mental status and physiologic trends matter.
寒冷暴露时，应使患者远离继续失热，擦干并隔热，轻柔搬动。外周温度计读数并不完美；意识及生理趋势很重要。

00:06:36.144 --> 00:06:47.544
The cold-water submersion station can involve both hypoxia and hypothermia. Continue to reassess breathing and perfusion instead of treating temperature as the only problem.
冷水浸没站点可能同时涉及缺氧与低体温。应持续复评呼吸及灌注，而非只处理温度。

00:06:47.544 --> 00:07:00.528
A rescuer must not enter unsafe water without the required training, flotation and rescue plan. Use appropriate rescue resources and maintain scene safety before patient contact.
救援人员不得在缺少所需训练、浮具及救援计划时进入不安全水域。接触患者前，应使用适当救援资源并确保现场安全。

00:07:00.528 --> 00:07:13.944
After removal, assess breathing, oxygenation, airway contamination, perfusion, temperature and mechanism-related trauma. Drowning may follow a medical event rather than cause it.
救出后评估呼吸、氧合、气道污染、灌注、体温及机制相关创伤；溺水可能是某种医疗事件的结果，而非起因。

00:07:13.944 --> 00:07:27.888
Current H12 directs care through the appropriate resuscitation pathway with particular attention to airway and oxygenation. Cold-water cases can require specialist consultation and continued resuscitation decisions.
现行H12要求按适当复苏路径处理，特别关注气道及氧合。冷水病例可能需要专业咨询及持续复苏决策。

00:07:27.888 --> 00:07:39.864
Fresh versus salt water does not create two field treatment recipes. A seemingly minor rescue may still have later respiratory risk, so follow current conveyance guidance.
淡水与海水不会形成两套现场治疗方案。看似轻微的救援之后仍有呼吸风险，应遵循现行转运指导。

00:07:39.864 --> 00:07:51.312
A mechanic is trapped under a collapsed vehicle lift in a cold garage. The compression duration is uncertain; the lower leg is swollen and the patient is pale and anxious.
一名机械师被困在寒冷车库倒塌的汽车升降机下。受压时间不确定；小腿肿胀，患者面色苍白且焦虑。

00:07:51.312 --> 00:08:07.200
The team verifies machinery and structural stability, obtains rescue resources, identifies access/egress and reports the entrapment time as uncertain. The release is a coordinated operation, not a spontaneous pull.
团队核实机械及结构稳定性、请求救援资源、确认进出路线，并把受困时间报告为不确定。解除压迫是协调行动，不是突然拉人。

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:19.464
Use the current H02 pathway and required consultation to plan what is feasible before release. Anticipate systemic deterioration and prepare monitoring and reassessment.
依现行H02路径及所需咨询计划解除前可做的事，并预期全身恶化，准备监测和复评。

00:08:19.464 --> 00:08:31.536
The case does not supply a universal fluid amount or automatic tourniquet rule. Mechanism, duration, muscle burden, hemodynamics and provider authorization shape the plan.
本例不提供通用液体量或自动止血带规则。机制、时长、受累肌肉量、血流动力学及执业者权限共同决定计划。

00:08:31.536 --> 00:08:46.032
Before moving, decide whether the patient can assist and whether a lift, carry, slide or evacuation device is appropriate. Check the route for stairs, turns, weather, contaminated surfaces and obstacles.
搬动前要判断患者能否配合，以及抬举、搬运、滑移或撤离器材是否适用；检查楼梯、转角、天气、污染表面及障碍物。

00:08:46.032 --> 00:08:58.176
Assign a clear leader and one coordinated count. Protect airway access, oxygen, bleeding control, temperature measures and monitoring from being unintentionally disconnected.
明确一名负责人并使用统一口令。防止气道、氧气、止血、温度处理及监测在搬动中意外中断。

00:08:58.176 --> 00:09:08.640
Reassess immediately after packaging or movement. A new breathing problem, loss of pulse quality, increased pain or displaced device changes the plan.
固定或搬动后应立即复评。新发呼吸问题、脉搏质量下降、疼痛加重或器材移位都将改变计划。

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:20.928
The saved outline asks learners to make a rapid thirty-second load-and-go decision. Treat this as a school verbalization exercise to surface priorities, not an operational stopwatch law.
学校纲要要求在30秒内作出快速装车决策。应将其视为口头优先级训练，而非临床操作计时法规。

00:09:20.928 --> 00:09:34.536
State the threat, the reason transport cannot wait, the minimum safe preparation and who will continue care during movement. Identify any rescue or extrication step that must happen first.
说明威胁、不能等待的转运理由、最低限度安全准备，以及搬动中谁继续照护；并指出是否必须先完成救援或脱困。

00:09:34.536 --> 00:09:46.248
A rapid decision is not a rushed move. Package safely, maintain airway and hemorrhage priorities, secure equipment and reassess after each major change.
快速决策不等于仓促搬动。应安全固定、维持气道及止血优先事项、固定器材，并在每次重大变化后复评。

00:09:46.248 --> 00:10:14.856
This fire-exposed patient has hoarseness, soot and increasing effort. Airway deterioration and combustion toxicity are immediate concerns. I recommend rapid conveyance with indicated oxygen and early higher-level support. Before moving, confirm a safe route, secure the patient and equipment, and assign airway observation. Reassess after movement, and send a pre-alert with actual care and response.
这位火灾暴露患者有嘶哑、烟灰及呼吸用力增加，气道恶化和燃烧毒物是即时担忧。我建议快速转运，同时给予有指征氧疗并及早请求更高层级支持。移动前确认安全路线，固定患者及器材，并指定气道观察人员；移动后复评，预警时报告实际处理与反应。

00:10:14.856 --> 00:10:42.456
That is an original worked decision, not a school answer or a new diagnosis. It names the threat, choice, essential preparation and continuing care. Say it in your own words and time the rehearsal against the school’s thirty-second target. If breathing is inadequate, indicated ventilation cannot wait for completion of a speech or loading. Revise the plan when new findings or rescue conditions change.
这是原创决策示范，不是学校答案或新增诊断。它说明威胁、选择、必要准备及持续照护。应改用自己的话，在演练中按学校30秒目标计时。通气不足时，有指征通气不能等讲话或装车完成；新发现或救援条件变化时，必须修订计划。

00:10:42.456 --> 00:10:54.456
After each station, say what the task was testing, what you observed, what action you took and what changed. A score without a reasoned debrief can hide an unsafe shortcut.
每个站点结束后，应说清考核目的、观察内容、采取行动及结果变化。只有分数而没有推理复盘，可能掩盖不安全捷径。

00:10:54.456 --> 00:11:06.624
Ask the instructor to clarify the official sequence, device model, time target and documentation requirement. Do not infer an unknown school rubric from a generic textbook.
请教师说明正式步骤、器材型号、计时目标及记录要求。不能从通用教材推断未知学校评分标准。

00:11:06.624 --> 00:11:17.448
Repeat the station until the skill is both safe and reproducible. Narrated preparation supports practice but cannot replace witnessed competency sign-off.
反复练习，直到技能既安全又可重复。配音准备可以支持练习，但不能替代现场观察的能力签核。
